{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The local group `remote-access` exists on node1 and `opsadmin` is a member.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The group and previously absent account were created, membership was directly observed, and the same account/group state remained after reboot and final cleanup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac09a52c4ff74e38","cmd-c9dbcd0565ac4208","cmd-40d2a65cceb745f8","cmd-e31b781650a04cc1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"SSH login access on node1 is restricted to members of `remote-access`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective sshd policy was `AllowGroups remote-access`. Real SSH tests showed `opsadmin`, a member, succeeding and a credentialed non-member being denied, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2af3e3107314f34","cmd-6a5afa7c48a848e7","cmd-56c3a009a2f2434c","cmd-e31b781650a04cc1"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/group provisioning and the sshd policy directly implemented the task. Temporary probe accounts, keys, trackers, and authorized-key changes had a bounded behavioral-verification role and were removed or restored. The scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, the expected socket set, and only normal reboot-generated temporary-directory churn.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9dbcd0565ac4208","cmd-c2af3e3107314f34","cmd-890940587a5e4180","cmd-7477342a80384566","cmd-eacf058f0f174d7d","cmd-4289892849de4b6d","cmd-e31b781650a04cc1","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, its boot ID changed from e65e6bcf-e09d-42b7-8317-cb6310086cb7 to 32b88061-15b9-4001-9992-1d1f0a620fad, and sshd, policy, account/group state, network listening, and allow/deny behavior recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm that transition.","limitations":[]}
